jU1OTA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16255906?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/v1993","html_url":"https://github.com/v1993","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v1993/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v1993/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v1993/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v1993/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v1993/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v1993/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v1993/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v1993/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v1993/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-29T10:46:09Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T10:46:09Z","body":"I think this is still incorrect: you need to subtract the result travel length *before* projecting as it represents motion up to the point of collision. This seems like the proper fix (3D version):\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nif (first_slide) {\r\n\treal_t remainder_magnitude = motion.length() - result.travel.length();\r\n\tVector3 remainder_adjusted = result.remainder.normalized() * remainder_magnitude\r\n\tmotion = remainder_adjusted.slide(wall_normal);\r\n} else {\r\n\tmotion = result.remainder.slide(wall_normal);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere's also a case where you were just ejected from a wall as part of collision recovery but are moving away from it and thus should skip sliding entirely; here's code to account for that too (again, 3D version):\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nif (first_slide) {\r\n\treal_t remainder_magnitude = motion.length() - result.travel.length();\r\n\tVector3 remainder_adjusted = result.remainder.normalized() * remainder_magnitude\r\n\tif (result.remainder.dot(wall_normal) <= 0.0) {\r\n\t\tmotion = remainder_adjusted.slide(wall_normal);\r\n\t} else {\r\n\t\tmotion = remainder_adjusted\r\n\t}\r\n} else {\r\n\tmotion = result.remainder.slide(wall_normal);\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4342978741/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]